Start the Cassini core driver (cxi-ss1) with its headers: the register
and counter definitions, error definitions, telemetry item tables, and
the CXI interface (cxi.h, cxi_prov_hw.h, libcassini.h) through which
client drivers use the NIC.

The cassini_* headers are generated from the hardware description and
are not meant to be edited by hand, so they carry the generator's
formatting.  cassini_user_defs.h is shared byte-for-byte with the user
space libraries and is therefore under include/uapi/ethernet.  It
provides inline accessors that need errno.h, string.h and size_t,
which a standalone UAPI header cannot assume, so this patch excludes
it from the UAPI header self-test.

All fixed-width types use the kernel names (u8..u64) as the headers
are consumed from kernel code.

The Kconfig and Makefile hookup for this driver is deliberately the
last patch of the driver group, so that every earlier patch adds
sources without changing what the tree builds.

Known limitation, deferred to V2: this patch carries SR-IOV
virtual-function code (VF-to-PF mailbox requests, mailbox opcodes or VF
resource handling) from an older, incomplete version of the Cassini
SR-IOV support. V2 of this series will include the updated SR-IOV
implementation, so issues in the VF paths should be ignored for now.

